From: vegetableleaf <benzhu2029@u.northwestern.edu>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 13:22:34 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] CF-CLONE-3: a pulled unit is set up as a clone from its
 pulled state

The refusal "leaves a pulled state for a clone's setup, not modelled" (GridStateSetter.exitPulled) is removed: a Clone
reaching a Fisherman his hook drags to a building, or a troop a hook pulls, sets it up from the pulled state. The exit
runs as for any other state (components on, the point, move time, charge and pushback reset, a reference out of
range dropped, the standing test), and the clone setup's entry empties the route. The unit then follows the hook no
more: its state visit follows only in a pulled state, and a hook on a building drags its owner only while he is in
his, so the hook flies on dragging nothing and is let go at its aim; a pulled troop's hook flies back without it and
is let go short of the Fisherman, who goes on. Not traced from the client nor held by a recording (b): the exit and
the hook's step as crforge has them.

BattleFishermanTest: the refusal test of a pulled troop asked into a clone's setup becomes two scenes, a dragged
Fisherman cloned and a pulled Knight cloned by its own side's Clone.
